;; expect: main.f refused unknown_head
;; §8.4 slice 3.18 rule 1: a row's type is never an E inductive. This body is E-first (it
;; calls `tag`, a fn over a Symbol, E only — an extern was the trigger until slice 4.3 landing 1
;; gave externs an L meaning), and the classifier does not know ByteArray.mk: no E-first function
;; builds a cell where the typed route passes the bare field, so the two routes cannot disagree
;; on a ByteArray's representation. The remedy is a typed function that packs (row_types' `pack`)
(import Init String.toByteArray)
(fn tag ((s Symbol)) Nat 0)
(fn f ((l (List UInt8))) ByteArray (match (tag (quote x)) (_ (ByteArray.mk (Array.mk l)))))
